Upstream-Status: Pending

The neutron platform driver's probe() calls neutron_get_rproc() exactly
once and caches the result in ndev->rproc permanently, even on failure.
On this board imx_neutron_rproc registers remoteproc0 a few milliseconds
*after* neutron's probe() runs, so rproc_get_by_phandle() returns NULL
and ndev->rproc is left NULL forever -- it is never retried.

neutron_rproc_boot() then only checks IS_ERR(rproc), which does not
catch a plain NULL pointer (IS_ERR(NULL) is false), so execution falls
through to atomic_read(&rproc->power) and dereferences NULL. The first
process to open /dev/neutronN after boot crashes the kernel with a
level-0 translation fault in neutron_rproc_boot/neutron_open.

Retry the rproc lookup if it has not yet been resolved, and reject a
NULL handle in addition to an encoded error pointer.

--- a/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_device.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/neutron/neutron_device.c
@@ -306,10 +306,10 @@

 int neutron_rproc_boot(struct neutron_device *ndev, const char *fw_name)
 {
-	struct rproc *rproc = ndev->rproc;
+	struct rproc *rproc = ndev->rproc ? ndev->rproc : (ndev->rproc = neutron_get_rproc(ndev));
 	int ret = 0;

-	if (IS_ERR(rproc))
+	if (!rproc || IS_ERR(rproc))
 		return -ENODEV;

 	if (atomic_read(&rproc->power) == 0) {
